{
  "name": "Webhook: create a Social Poster draft from a shop or form request, optionally scheduled",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d962dd4e-ace7-5e0a-baaf-c5b0a71f3d25",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -320,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nThe workflow accepts an HTTP POST from a shop, form or other app. If there is no text in `caption`, `text` or `message`, it answers with status 400. Otherwise it takes the link, title and public media URLs, saves the post with “Create the draft” and answers with the draft id.\n\n### Draft or scheduled\nThe default is `mode` = `draft`: the workflow only creates a draft and schedules or publishes nothing. The link to view it is in the output of “Create the draft” under `draft.app_draft_url`. To schedule posts, set `mode` to `schedule`. “Schedule the draft” then schedules it `minutesFromNow` minutes later (at least 5) and confirms it. If your team requires approval, it waits under “Waiting for you”. There is no immediate publishing. If the request sends `\"schedule\": false`, it stays a draft even then.\n\n### Setup\nThis template uses the unverified community node `n8n-nodes-social-poster` (tested with version 0.1.1). It runs on self-hosted n8n only, not on n8n Cloud. Install it under Settings → Community Nodes → Install. Guide: https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/\nCreate “Social Poster API” credentials. You get the key in Social Poster under the account menu → AI access → API key for n8n. The base URL is `https://app.social-poster.io` without `/mcp`.\nEnter your account reference (`acc_…`) in “Settings and fields”. Save the workflow, copy the production webhook URL and send `{\"caption\":\"Test post\"}`. If n8n is reachable from the internet, protect the webhook, for example with Header Auth. Never put the API key in the request.\n\n### Customization\nYou can rename the fields to match your form.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 680,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "69584216-4f27-5d9f-ba94-f9166ee6eda6",
      "name": "Receive the request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        460,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Webhook and checks\nOnly requests with a caption continue. Requests without text receive status 400.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2bde1094-aa59-56dd-9ad3-2a300360faac",
      "name": "Map the fields",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1020,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Account and content\nAccount reference, `mode` (default `draft`) and `minutesFromNow` live here. The caption comes from the request.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "05b245ce-2093-5951-804f-7d108bbce0d2",
      "name": "Draft or schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1560,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Draft, optionally scheduled\nEvery request becomes a draft. Only with `mode` = `schedule` and no `schedule` false does “Schedule the draft” schedule it. The answer contains the draft id.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 820,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c83dc518-e393-5b26-8c9c-ca63006b67a4",
      "name": "Protect the webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        460,
        800
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "If n8n is reachable from the internet, add authentication on the Webhook node. Never send the Social Poster key in the request.",
        "height": 150,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
